PREFACE

  Regulation 5 of 2009

  Regulation establishing the Hesperian Data Protection Board

  Regulation of the Assembly of the Hesperian Union and of the Hesperian Council establishing the Hesperian Data Protection Board, laying down its composition, tasks and powers, and providing for the consistent supervision of cross-border processing of personal data within the Union.

PREAMBLE

  Having regard to the Treaty establishing the Hesperian Union, and in particular Article 41 thereof,

  Having regard to the proposal from the Hesperian Commission,

  Whereas:

  (1) Directive 12 of 2004 requires each member state to establish one or more independent supervisory authorities and requires those authorities to cooperate in order to secure the consistent application of that Directive throughout the Union.

  (2) Experience of the operation of Directive 12 of 2004 has shown that cooperation between national supervisory authorities is more effective where it is coordinated by a standing body of the Union endowed with legal personality.

  (3) A body should therefore be established, to be known as the Hesperian Data Protection Board, to contribute to the consistent application of the rules on the protection of personal data across the Union and to advise the Commission on matters relating to such protection.

  (4) In order to ensure that the rules governing the Board apply uniformly and take effect at the same time throughout the Union, those rules should be laid down in a regulation, which is directly applicable and does not require transposition into national law.

  (5) The Board should be independent in the performance of its tasks, and its members should neither seek nor take instructions from any government or other body.

  THE ASSEMBLY OF THE HESPERIAN UNION AND THE HESPERIAN COUNCIL, Having regard to the Treaty establishing the Hesperian Union, HAS ADOPTED THIS REGULATION:

BODY

CHAPTER 1 - ESTABLISHMENT AND TASKS

  ARTICLE 1 - Subject matter

    This Regulation establishes the Hesperian Data Protection Board and lays down its composition, tasks, powers and working arrangements.

  ARTICLE 2 - Definitions

    For the purposes of this Regulation, the definitions in Article 3 of Directive 12 of 2004 apply, and in addition—

    POINT (a)

      "the Board" means the Hesperian Data Protection Board established by Article 3;

    POINT (b)

      "cross-border processing" means processing of personal data which takes place in the context of the activities of establishments in more than one member state, or which substantially affects data subjects in more than one member state;

    POINT (c)

      "lead supervisory authority" means the supervisory authority of the member state in which the controller has its main establishment.

  ARTICLE 3 - Establishment and legal personality

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      The Hesperian Data Protection Board is hereby established.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      The Board shall have legal personality, and shall enjoy in each member state the most extensive legal capacity accorded to legal persons under national law.

    PARAGRAPH (3)

      The Board shall be represented by its Chair.

  ARTICLE 4 - Independence

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      The Board shall act with complete independence in performing its tasks and exercising its powers.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      In the performance of its tasks the Board shall neither seek nor take instructions from any government, institution of the Union, or other body.

  ARTICLE 5 - Tasks of the Board

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      The Board shall ensure the consistent application of Directive 12 of 2004, and to that end shall—

      POINT (a)

        monitor and promote the consistent application of that Directive throughout the Union;

      POINT (b)

        advise the Commission on any matter relating to the protection of personal data in the Union;

      POINT (c)

        issue guidelines, recommendations and statements of best practice for the guidance of supervisory authorities; and

      POINT (d)

        promote cooperation and the effective exchange of information between supervisory authorities.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      Where a competent supervisory authority intends to adopt a measure concerning cross-border processing, the Board may issue an opinion in accordance with Article 9.

  ARTICLE 6 - Reports

    The Board shall draw up an annual report on the protection of natural persons with regard to processing in the Union, and shall make the report public and transmit it to the Assembly of the Hesperian Union, the Council and the Commission.

CHAPTER 2 - COMPOSITION AND PROCEDURE

  ARTICLE 7 - Composition

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      The Board shall be composed of the head of one supervisory authority of each member state.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      Where a member state has more than one supervisory authority, that member state shall designate a joint representative.

  ARTICLE 8 - Chair

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      The Board shall elect a Chair and two Deputy Chairs from among its members by a simple majority.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      The term of office of the Chair and of each Deputy Chair shall be five years, renewable once.

  ARTICLE 9 - Consistency opinions

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      Where a matter of general application raises a question as to the consistent application of Directive 12 of 2004, the Board shall issue an opinion, provided that the matter has been referred to it by a supervisory authority, by the Chair or by the Commission.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      The competent supervisory authorities shall take utmost account of the opinion of the Board, and shall inform the Chair whether they will maintain or amend the measure to which the opinion relates.

  ARTICLE 10 - Dispute resolution

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      Where a lead supervisory authority and another supervisory authority concerned hold conflicting views on the handling of a case of cross-border processing, the Board shall adopt a binding decision.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      A decision under paragraph (1) shall be adopted by a two-thirds majority of the members of the Board, and shall be reasoned and addressed to the supervisory authorities concerned.

  ARTICLE 11 - Voting

    Save where this Regulation provides otherwise, the Board shall take decisions by a simple majority of its members, and the Chair shall have a casting vote in the event of a tie.

  ARTICLE 12 - Rules of procedure

    The Board shall adopt its own rules of procedure by a two-thirds majority of its members and shall organise its own operational arrangements.

  ARTICLE 13 - Secretariat

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      The Board shall have a secretariat, which shall be provided by the Commission.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      The secretariat shall perform its tasks exclusively under the instructions of the Chair of the Board.

  ARTICLE 14 - Confidentiality

    The members of the Board and its secretariat shall be subject to a duty of professional secrecy with regard to confidential information which comes to their knowledge in the course of the performance of their tasks, both during and after their term of office.

  ARTICLE 15 - Professional secrecy of information

    Information exchanged between supervisory authorities and the Board under this Regulation and used for the purpose of a consistency opinion or a binding decision shall be subject to the duty of professional secrecy and shall not be disclosed except with the consent of the authority which provided it.

  ARTICLE 16 - Cooperation with the Commission

    The Board shall keep the Commission informed of its activities, and the Commission may attend the meetings of the Board without the right to vote.

  ARTICLE 17 - Review

    By 31 December 2014, and every five years thereafter, the Commission shall submit a report on the operation of this Regulation to the Assembly of the Hesperian Union and to the Council, accompanied where appropriate by proposals for its amendment.

  ARTICLE 18 - Entry into force and application

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the Hesperian Union.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      This Regulation shall be binding in its entirety and directly applicable in all member states.
